[63.527167, "o", "\r\u001b[2K\r\n\u001b[1;31mmini-swe-agent\u001b[0m\u001b[31m (step \u001b[0m\u001b[1;31m4\u001b[0m\u001b[31m, \u001b[0m\u001b[1;31m$0.00\u001b[0m\u001b[31m):\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[32m⠦\u001b[0m Waiting for the LM to respond...\r\u001b[2KThere is no GPU available, so training must be CPU-efficient. I’ll install a CPU-compatible PyTorch stack plus PEFT 0.15.0 and the required Hugging Face \r\nlibraries.\r\n\r\n```\r\ncd /app && df -h . 2>/dev/null || true; pip install --no-cache-dir torch 'transformers>=4.40,<5' 'peft==0.15.0' 'accelerate>=0.30' datasets 2>&1 | tail -40\r\n```\r\n\u001b[32m⠦\u001b[0m Waiting for the LM to respond...\r\u001b[2K\u001b[32m⠦\u001b[0m Waiting for the LM to respond...\r\n\u001b[?25h\r\u001b[1A\u001b[2K"]
