[269.287836, "o", "\r\u001b[2KGPT-2 loads and a single backward pass is feasible. I’ll benchmark realistic batch sizes and sequence lengths to estimate training time, then write the training\r\nscript accordingly.\r\n\r\n```\r\ncd /app && python - <<'PY'\r\nimport torch, time, json\r\nfrom transformers import AutoTokenizer, AutoModelForCausalLM\r\ntorch.set_num_threads(20)\r\ntok=AutoTokenizer.from_pretrained('openai-community/gpt2'); tok.pad_token=tok.eos_token\r\nmodel=AutoModelForCausalLM.from_pretrained('openai-community/gpt2')\r\nsamples=json.load(open('data/train.json'))\r\ndef prompt(s):\r\n    opts='\\n'.join(s['options'])\r\n    return f\"Question: {s['question']}\\n{opts}\\nAnswer:\"\r\nlens=[len(tok(prompt(s)+' '+s['answer']).input_ids) for s in samples]\r\nimport numpy as np\r\nprint('token lengths min/mean/p95/max',min(lens),sum(lens)/len(lens),np.percentile(lens,95),max(lens))\r\nfor bs in [4,8,16]:\r\n    batch=[tok(prompt(s)+' '+s['answer'], padding='max_length', max_length=192, truncation=True, return_tensors='pt') for s in samples[:bs]]\r\n    ids=torch.st"]
[269.287858, "o", "ack([b.input_ids[0] for b in batch]); mask=torch.stack([b.attention_mask[0] for b in batch])\r\n    labels=ids.clone()\r\n    model.train(); t=time.time(); out=model(input_ids=ids, attention_mask=mask, labels=labels); loss=out.loss; loss.backward(); dt=time.time()-t\r\n    print('bs',bs,'time',round(dt,2),'loss',loss.item())\r\nPY\r\n```\r\n\u001b[32m⠼\u001b[0m Waiting for the LM to respond..."]
