[610.190246, "o", "\r\u001b[2K\u001b[32m⠴\u001b[0m Waiting for the LM to respond...\r\u001b[2K\r\n\u001b[1;31mmini-swe-agent\u001b[0m\u001b[31m (step \u001b[0m\u001b[1;31m25\u001b[0m\u001b[31m, \u001b[0m\u001b[1;31m$0.00\u001b[0m\u001b[31m):\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[32m⠴\u001b[0m Waiting for the LM to respond..."]
[610.197237, "o", "\r\u001b[2KThe benchmark shows CPU throughput is essentially insensitive to thread count, and ~128 tokens at batch size 8 is a reasonable speed/context tradeoff. I’ll \r\nrestart training for up to 5 epochs with early stopping and monitor progress.\r\n\r\n```\r\ncd /app && kill $(cat bench.pid) 2>/dev/null || true; sleep 1; kill -9 $(cat bench.pid) 2>/dev/null || true\r\npython - <<'PY'\r\np='train_lora.py'\r\ns=open(p).read()\r\ns=s.replace('parser.add_argument(\"--epochs\", type=int, default=10)', 'parser.add_argument(\"--epochs\", type=int, default=5)')\r\ns=s.replace('parser.add_argument(\"--max_length\", type=int, default=256)', 'parser.add_argument(\"--max_length\", type=int, default=128)')\r\ns=s.replace('parser.add_argument(\"--patience\", type=int, default=3)', 'parser.add_argument(\"--patience\", type=int, default=2)')\r\ns=s.replace('torch.set_num_threads(min(20, os.cpu_count() or 1))', 'torch.set_num_threads(2)')\r\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\r\nPY\r\npython -m py_compile train_lora.py && rm -rf experiments/lora_adapter lora_results.json && OMP_N"]
[610.197561, "o", "UM_THREADS=2 MKL_NUM_THREADS=2 nohup python train_lora.py > \r\n/app/train_lora.log 2>&1 & echo $! > /app/train_lora.pid; echo restarted $(cat /app/train_lora.pid); sleep 5; tail -10 train_lora.log\r\n```\r\n\u001b[32m⠴\u001b[0m Waiting for the LM to respond..."]
[610.198044, "o", "\r\u001b[2K\u001b[32m⠴\u001b[0m Waiting for the LM to respond...\r\n\u001b[?25h\r\u001b[1A\u001b[2K"]
