[844.599496, "o", "\r\u001b[2K\r\n\u001b[1;31mmini-swe-agent\u001b[0m\u001b[31m (step \u001b[0m\u001b[1;31m33\u001b[0m\u001b[31m, \u001b[0m\u001b[1;31m$0.00\u001b[0m\u001b[31m):\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[32m⠴\u001b[0m Waiting for the LM to respond..."]
[844.603108, "o", "\r\u001b[2KAfter one epoch validation accuracy is only 22%, so the adapter needs more optimization or a better training signal. I’ll compute the validation-set surface \r\nbaselines while the next epoch runs, to know what performance is realistically achievable.\r\n\r\n```\r\ncd /app && python - <<'PY'\r\nimport json\r\nfrom collections import Counter\r\nfor split in ['train','val']:\r\n d=json.load(open(f'data/{split}.json'))\r\n n=len(d)\r\n longest=sum(sorted([len(o) for o in s['options']], reverse=True).index(len(s['options'][ord(s['answer'])-65]))==0 for s in d)\r\n mostwords=sum(sorted([len(o.split()) for o in s['options']], reverse=True).index(len(s['options'][ord(s['answer'])-65].split()))==0 for s in d)\r\n always=max(Counter(s['answer'] for s in d).values())\r\n print(split, 'longest-char', longest/n, 'longest-words', mostwords/n, 'majority', always/n, Counter(s['answer'] for s in d))\r\n# option ordinal stats conditioned on answer\r\nfor split in ['train','val']:\r\n d=json.load(open(f'data/{split}.json'))\r\n print(split)\r\n for a in '"]
[844.60326, "o", "ABCD':\r\n  n=sum(s['answer']==a for s in d)\r\n  longest=sum(ord(s['answer'])-65==max(range(4),key=lambda i:len(s['options'][i])) for s in d if s['answer']==a)\r\n  print(a,n,'longest among that answer',longest/n if n else 0)\r\nPY\r\necho '--- training log ---'; tail -10 train_lora.log\r\n```\r\n\u001b[32m⠴\u001b[0m Waiting for the LM to respond...\r\u001b[2K\u001b[32m⠴\u001b[0m Waiting for the LM to respond...\r\n\u001b[?25h\r\u001b[1A\u001b[2K"]
