[1108.280121, "o", "\r\u001b[2KValidation accuracy is stuck at exactly 22%, which equals the validation prevalence of letter A and suggests the adapter collapsed to a single output token. \r\nI’ll stop training, inspect its predictions, and then restart with option-shuffle augmentation and stronger regularization to prevent this collapse.\r\n\r\n```\r\ncd /app && kill $(cat train_lora.pid) 2>/dev/null || true; sleep 1; kill -9 $(cat train_lora.pid) 2>/dev/null || true; cat > /app/diag.py <<'PY'\r\nimport json, torch, re\r\nfrom collections import Counter\r\nfrom transformers import AutoTokenizer, AutoModelForCausalLM\r\nfrom peft import PeftModel\r\ntok=AutoTokenizer.from_pretrained('/app/experiments/lora_adapter')\r\nbase=AutoModelForCausalLM.from_pretrained('openai-community/gpt2')\r\nmodel=PeftModel.from_pretrained(base,'/app/experiments/lora_adapter'); model.eval()\r\nva=json.load(open('/app/data/val.json'))\r\nids=[tok(' '+x, add_special_tokens=False).input_ids[0] for x in 'ABCD']\r\npreds=[]; gold=[]\r\nfor s in va:\r\n p='Question: '+s['question']+'\\n'+'\\n'"]
[1108.280202, "o", ".join(s['options'])+'\\nAnswer:'\r\n enc=tok(p, return_tensors='pt', truncation=True, max_length=128)\r\n with torch.no_grad(): out=model(**enc)\r\n logits=out.logits[0,-1,ids]\r\n pred='ABCD'[int(logits.argmax())]\r\n preds.append(pred); gold.append(s['answer'])\r\nprint('acc',sum(a==b for a,b in zip(preds,gold))/len(gold))\r\nprint('preds',Counter(preds))\r\nprint('gold',Counter(gold))\r\nprint('confusion')\r\nfor a in 'ABCD':\r\n print(a, {b:sum(1 for x,y in zip(gold,preds) if x==a and y==b) for b in 'ABCD'})\r\nPY\r\nOMP_NUM_THREADS=2 nohup python /app/diag.py > /app/diag.log 2>&1 & echo $! > /app/diag.pid; echo diag_started\r\n```\r\n\u001b[32m⠼\u001b[0m Waiting for the LM to respond...\r\u001b[2K\u001b[32m⠼\u001b[0m Waiting for the LM to respond...\r\n\u001b[?25h\r\u001b[1A\u001b[2K"]
[1109.29791, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;32mTool\u001b[0m:\r\n"]
[1109.297974, "o", "<returncode>\r\n0\r\n<output>\r\ndiag_started\r\n\r\n"]
